# Paths jcode must not read.
#
# Gitignore syntax. jcode reads .jcodeignore first if it exists, then this file.
#
# WHY: every file the agent reads is re-billed as input tokens on every later
# turn of the conversation, so one accidental read of a large generated file is
# a tax on the whole session, not a one-off cost. Measured on 2026-08-27:
# sessions reaching 400k+ context accounted for 44% of all token spend.
#
# This is a cost guard, NOT a security boundary: `bash` can still cat these
# paths. Secrets belong in Doppler, not behind an ignore file.
#
# Enforced by: read, ls, agentgrep (grep and find modes).

# --- Build output. Regenerated from source, never worth reading. ---
target/
dist/
build/
.next/
out/

# --- Dependencies. Read the manifest, never the vendored tree. ---
node_modules/
vendor/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Lock files. Enormous, and the manifest carries the intent. ---
Cargo.lock
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
uv.lock
poetry.lock

# --- Generated or machine-authored. AGENTS.md forbids hand-editing these. ---
CHANGELOG.md
*.min.js
*.min.css
*.map

# --- Binary and media: unreadable as text, expensive to attempt. ---
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.ico
*.pdf
*.zip
*.gz
*.tar
*.wasm
*.dylib
*.so
*.a
*.rlib

# --- Local scratch and caches, including this repo's own conventions. ---
.local/
scratch/
tmp/
.cache/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
coverage/

# --- Test fixture corpora: large, repetitive, low signal per token. ---
crates/*/src/tool/testdata/
**/snapshots/

# --- Secrets: never in context, even though bash could still reach them. ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
auth.json
credentials.json
